Subject: Fix: Shy Guy's blue Peach kit is made, the disc's is unfinished (issue #176)
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A fix of the original game's data, always on and without a switch, like the
other fixes in this series.

Peach has a blue kit on the disc (peach_alt.rlt, her goalie's and one for each
of the eight sidekicks), which CharacterLoader loads for a captain against a
captain of his colours. No captain shares Peach's colour, so the retail game
never shows it; Blue Peach (tweak patch 0017) and Mirror match (0015, and a
set's mirror match, 0062) do. Seven of the sidekick kits are finished: her
pink turns blue (#E2578B to #5CB8FE, her away colour) and her light blue turns
yellow (#67B6F9 to #FFF422). Shy Guy's (shyguy_peach_alt.rlt) never was: it is
red and yellow with Petey's green emblem, closest to shyguy_petey_alt.rlt.
The file is the same on the US, European (both revisions), Japanese and Korean
discs.

When a sidekick bundle holds that texture with the disc's bytes,
FinalizeLoadingSidekickSwapTexture now makes it before the bundle registers:
src/platform/away_kits.cpp copies Shy Guy's pink Peach kit (shyguy_peach.rlt)
into it and recolours it as the seven finished kits are. Team texels are those
that differ from Luigi's and Wario's versions of the texture; pink ones take
the blue, light blue ones the yellow, everything else keeps its bytes. The
three files are read from the disc as the kit loads. A texture with other
bytes (a changed file) is left alone. A texture pack's HD image of the pink
kit is not used for it: the made kit keeps the game's resolution.

